      "page": 1,
      "text": "HT-8\nEightballers\nCDR D. Burkett NAS WHITING FIELD, FL CDR S. Kohl\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nTraining the World's Best Helicopter Pilots\nSaturday, 14-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 06:14 MOONRISE: 10:52 % ILLUM: 21% JULIAN DATE: 6318\nSUNSET: 16:51 MOONSET: 21:10\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 0 TOTAL FLY HRS: 0.0\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 10 TOTAL SIM HRS: 15.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: HYDRAULIC SYSTEM NO.1 OR NO. 2 PRESSURE LOSS (TH-73)\nGeneral: What altitude restrictions are associated with operations at OLF Harold?\nNATOPS: What factors aggravate power required exceeding power available?\nSOP: Solo aircraft shall have their aircraft in what lighting configuration?\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nFDO LT ASTORGA B 0700 0659\nDUTY DRIVER 1stLt QUISPE M 0730 0729\nAM SDO ENS MAHONEY T 0700 1900\nPM SDO 1stLt GRAVES H 1900 0700\n***** Notes *****\nSouth Field NO CTO 0700 \u2013\nNavy Gas Mask Fitting: NITE Lab RM3, 09NOV \u2013 20NOV\n1500\n(0800 \u2013 1600)\nCTO 1500 - 2300\nKNSE & KNGS TACAN UNAVAILABLE 09NOV \u2013 18NOV\nPace 0815 \u2013 SUNSET\n***** Upcoming Events *****\nSpencer 0815 \u2013 SUNSET\nSanta Rosa 0815 \u2013 SUNSET\nHarold 0815 \u2013 SUNSET\nSite X 0815 \u2013 2245\nChoctaw CLOSED\nSTANDING NOTES:\n1. Snivels shall be in T-SHARP NLT 0800, two working days prior to the date of the snivel. Late snivels require a T-SHARP\nentry followed by verbal notification to the Operations Duty Officer. Late snivels will be handled on a case-by-case basis.\n2. All CAIs and MIL Classes are accessed via T-SHARP: https://tsharp.navsea.cloud.navy.mil . Students are responsible for\nensuring all prerequisite CAIs are completed prior to scheduled events.\n3. All are highly encouraged to complete SAFREP if a notable event occurs: https://saferep.safety.af.mil/\n4. Access publications via Eightball University: https://www.cnatra.navy.mil/tw5/ht8/university.asp or the HT-8 Sharepoint:\nhttps://flankspeed.sharepoint-mil.us/sites/HT-8Main/SitePages/HT8Home.aspx"
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "SAFETY OFFICER OPERATIONS OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER COMMANDING OFFICER\nD. MirandaHidalgo, Maj, USMC M. Dominik, LCDR, USNR S. Kohl, CDR, USN D. Burkett, CDR, USN\nFlight (Flight Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SCHD LNCH LAND INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nNUM TIME T/O LAND ICAO ICAO EVENT FLT\nTIME\nNo Flights Scheduled\nSimulator (Sim Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SIM/ INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nDEVICE\nNUM TIME T/O EVENT TIME\nL7U3-2 0700 0730 L7U3 CIV MURRAY M 1stLt DUELL C DAY2002A 1.5\nL7U5-2 0700 0730 L7U5 CIV KEYS R 2ndLt MATTEI M DAY2002A 1.5\nL7U6-3 0830 0900 L7U6 CIV JOHNSTONE J 1stLt REES B DAY3003A 1.5\nL7U2-3 0830 0900 L7U2 CIV HASKINS P ENS KLEISER H DAY3003A 1.5\nL7U1-4 1000 1030 L7U1 CIV ARMSTRONG W LTJG WONG K SAR3001R 1.5\nL7U6-4 1000 1030 L7U6 CIV COUREY J LTJG HARDY R SAR3001A 1.5\nL6U5-5 1130 1200 L6U5 CIV JOHNSTONE J 2ndLt ROBERTSON J DAY2001T 1.5\nL7U2-6 1300 1330 L7U2 CIV ARMSTRONG W LTJG SEARS J LND3001A 1.5\n(86(WU))\nL6U5-6 1300 1330 L6U5 CIV COUREY J 1stLt MICO D RI3201A 1.5\nL6U1-7 1430 1500 L6U1 CIV DIDIER D 1stLt MARTINEZ MONTES B DAY2001T 1.5\nGround Events\nTime Event Location Person Instructor Remarks\nNo Ground Events Scheduled"
